 <woodyst@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 12 Sep 2026 21:50:12 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: codecs: tfa9872: expose the total TDM speaker gain
 (TDMSPKG)

AMPGAIN alone changes the output level by only about 4.4 dB over 90 steps on the Nothing Phone (1).
Expose the other gain stage, TDMSPKG (TDM_CFG8 bits 9:6), as "Total Gain Volume" so it can be
measured and used for the call volume, whose audio never reaches the CPU.
---
 sound/soc/codecs/tfa9872.c | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/sound/soc/codecs/tfa9872.c b/sound/soc/codecs/tfa9872.c
index 7c1c6fb41..3e5f1a473 100644
--- a/sound/soc/codecs/tfa9872.c
+++ b/sound/soc/codecs/tfa9872.c
@@ -125,6 +125,12 @@ static const struct snd_soc_dapm_route tfa987x_dapm_routes[] = {
  */
 static const struct snd_kcontrol_new tfa987x_snd_controls[] = {
 	SOC_SINGLE("Amp Gain Volume", TFA987X_AMP_CFG, 5, 0xff, 0),
+	/*
+	 * TDMSPKG, the total speaker gain applied to the TDM input (TDM_CFG8 bits 9:6, 6 after reset).
+	 * AMPGAIN above moves the level by only ~4.4 dB over 90 steps on the Nothing Phone (1); this is the
+	 * other gain stage of the amplifier, to be measured as a call volume control.
+	 */
+	SOC_SINGLE("Total Gain Volume", TFA987X_TDM_CFG8, 6, 0xf, 0),
 };
 
 static const struct snd_soc_component_driver tfa987x_component = {
